ire medical intervention.", "ATROFIA:ATROFIA refers to the condition characterized by the reduction in size or wasting away of body tissues or organs. In the context of neuropathy, atrophy in the feet and hands can be a symptom associated with disorders that affect copper metabolism. Additionally, atrophy can also pertain to the reduction in size of the testicles, which may occur in cases of cryptorchidism. Thus, ATROFIA encompasses both peripheral atrophy related to neurological conditions and testicular atrophy linked to developmental issues.", "TORSIÓN TESTICULAR:Testicular torsion is a medical emergency that can occur in undescended testicles, leading to severe complications if not treated promptly.", "HADZISELIMOVIC:Hadziselimovic is a researcher who authored a debate on hormonal treatment of congenital undescended testes in a medical journal.", "TAY-SACHS DISEASE:Tay-Sachs disease is a neurodegenerative disorder caused by a deficiency of β-hexosaminidase A, affecting primarily Ashkenazi Jews.", "ENDOCRINOLOGY CONSULTATION:An endocrinology consultation was conducted for a 34-year-old patient referred for evaluation of bilateral gynecomastia.", "MUSCLE FATIGUE:Muscle fatigue is a significant symptom reported by the patient, indicating increasing difficulty in physical activities.", "HORMONAL STUDY:A hormonal study was requested to evaluate the patient's hormone levels, including FSH, LH, and testosterone.", "NEUROLOGY REFERRAL:The patient was referred to neurology for further study based on the findings from the endocrinology consultation.", "TUMORES TESTICULARES:Tumores testiculares son una categoría de cáncer que afecta a los testículos, incluyendo seminomas y no seminomas, y son responsables de la mayoría de los casos de cáncer testicular.", "SÍNDROME DE KENNEDY:El síndrome de Kennedy es una enfermedad rara que afecta a varones, caracterizada por debilidad muscular progresiva y atrofia, causada por una mutación genética en el receptor androgénico."], "paramet